        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "This works as expected and [is documented](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/bddfbfc4c1dbca6b852f512e554cf2e05c2960a8/doc/mini-clue.txt#L52-L58). The query keys in 'mini.starter' are implemented as buffer-local mappings to [`add_to_query()``](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/bddfbfc4c1dbca6b852f512e554cf2e05c2960a8/doc/mini-starter.txt#L593)\n\nThere are several possible solutions here:\n- Do not enable triggers in 'mini.starter' buffer (as is done by default). Mappings that don't start with [`query_updaters` character](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/bddfbfc4c1dbca6b852f512e554cf2e05c2960a8/doc/mini-starter.txt#L244) (like `<Space>`, for example) still work.\n- Redo selected 'mini.starter' buffer-local mappings after enabling triggers from 'mini.clue':\n   ```lua\n    vim.api.nvim_create_autocmd('User', {\n      pattern = 'MiniStarterOpened',\n      callback = function(event)\n        MiniClue.enable_buf_triggers(event.buf)\n        local map_query = function(key)\n          local rhs = function() MiniStarter.add_to_query(key, event.buf) end\n          vim.keymap.set('n', key, rhs, { buffer = event.buf, nowait = true })\n        end\n        map_query('g')\n        map_query('z')\n      end,\n    })\n   ``` ",
